    "narrative": "The focal point of today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** centers on the high-upside trio of **Corbin Carroll** (78.62), **James Wood** (76.28), and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98). **Corbin Carroll** remains a top-tier start against Keller, where his elite sprint speed and dynamic platoon splits against a right-handed arm provide a significant boost in our scarcest category, stolen bases. Meanwhile, **James Wood** is positioned for a monster outing; batting leadoff against Woods Richardson (4.85 xERA) grants him the highest volume of plate appearances and a massive +19% SP skill advantage. **Mickey Moniak** rounds out this tier, benefitting from an exceptional park factor (+14%) and a favorable hitting order position, making him a prime candidate to capitalize on the weak matchup against Scott.\n\nFor the remainder of the lineup, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) is our strongest infield play, buoyed by a wind-out projection and a solid platoon advantage. Conversely, **Trevor Story** presents a unique situation; while his raw score (52.39) is suppressed by an elite opposing arm in Jax (3.02 xERA), he is active primarily for his base-stealing utility against a slow-delivering pitcher, which we\u2019ve weighted heavily. We are closely monitoring the status of **Luis Campusano**, whose lineup position is currently pending; if he slides lower than the assumed 8-hole, his score will dip further, though his ability to exploit the platoon against Liberatore keeps him relevant. **Kyle Karros** (54.02) and **Travis Bazzana** (56.70) are marginal starts today, but they were kept in to maintain our daily efficiency floor.\n\nRegarding our bench, **Jose Caballero** remains the most significant exclusion. Despite possessing an impressive base projection of 59.45, he is currently omitted from the active lineup against Gore. While his speed profile is elite, the optimizer prioritized the platoon stability and order placement of our active starters over a bench asset who isn't currently confirmed to break the starting nine. As we look ahead to the full roster, including depth pieces like **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Cole Young**, we are effectively navigating a light day for our bench-locked stars like **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, and **Seiya Suzuki**, who are either on scheduled off-days or resting. We remain aggressive in the SB category, accepting the variance in the lower-scoring slots to ensure we don't leave potential stolen bases on the table.",
